        <p>Globalization and genre-bending define the present era. Tan Dun (China), A.R. Rahman (India), and Ryuichi Sakamoto (Japan) broke geographic barriers. Rock and electronic musicians entered the fold: Trent Reznor and Atticus Ross won for <em>The Social Network</em> (2010) and <em>Soul</em> (2020). Hildur Gu&eth;nad&oacute;ttir became the first solo woman to win (2019). First-time winners dominate&mdash;18 of 26 ceremonies&mdash;yet Ludwig G&ouml;ransson&rsquo;s three wins in eight years (2018, 2023, 2026) signal that a new dominant figure may be emerging. The era rewards stylistic individuality over orchestral convention.</p>
