      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>The 2020s are a pivot decade.</strong> With a 57% repeat-winner rate so far (4 of 7), the current decade could either settle into a new period of concentrated dominance (if G&ouml;ransson, Zimmer, or Reznor/Ross continue winning) or revert to the 2010s pattern of debut winners. The signal to watch: whether the next five ceremonies go to first-time or returning composers. The data supports both trajectories, making the late 2020s a genuinely uncertain inflection point.
      </li>
    </ol>
